{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1282519-my-experience-with-a-mastigos-awakening-character-background-nsfw","id":1282519,"title":"My experience with a Mastigos Awakening + Character background (NSFW)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-01-24T14:37:36-08:00","id":1282519,"title":"My experience with a Mastigos Awakening + Character background (NSFW)","content":"I've only recently joined a Mage: The Awakening campaign in a Dark Eras setting (ancient Hungary), and in the last session my character was awakened as a mage of Mastigos. The experience was possibly one of the trippiest things I've ever had described to me, and I honestly felt like I lost a couple points of Integrity IRL - to cut a long story short, during the &quot;nightmare&quot; of his Awakening, he had his fingers bitten off by some lady's vagina, had his ribs ripped open and played like a xylophone, and was turkey-slapped almost to death by his own magically-enlarged penis. This was all part of my character overcoming his Vice, which I will go into detail on below.<br /> <br /> Edmondo Huntsman is a travelling minstrel, loosely based on a similar character I've been playing in a separate Pathfinder campaign with another group. His stats are weighted more towards Social skills, with Expression (Music) being his most used skill/specialty. He recently acquired a rather exquisite lute from a fellow minstrel he knew from his bard school, after quite a bit of haggling on the price. His Virtue is &quot;Charming&quot;, and his Vice is &quot;Lustful&quot; - and yes, he's already engaged in his Vice on two separate occasions. Funnily enough, both times were when he was affected an injury of some kind. In the very first session, Edmondo had been stabbed by a street urchin who had stolen his coin pouch and fought back when he had tried to grapple him, and was promptly taken to the local healer's house. Upon realising that the healer was a) quite young, and b) rather attractive, Edmondo (AKA me) decided that it was time to have a crack at seeing how enacting his Vice would go. One exceptional success on a Presence + Persuasion check later, and as our GM described it, the stab wound in Edmondo's side wasn't the only hole being filled that night =).<br /> <br /> The second event was a few sessions later, and has somewhat more of a story attached to it - Edmondo and Federico (the street urchin who was now a member of our party) had eaten some meat infected with a parasite (which we would later find out only thrived in areas where dark magic was present, but that's not relevant here) and were rushed to the local healer's ward (a different village this time). The local healer, who was once again young and attractive, had prepared a drink of some sort from plants she had found in the wild, and given it to Federico and Edmondo to expel the parasites. Federico, having woken up before Edmondo, simply puked the parasites out, and although he felt a bit nauseous afterwards, he was otherwise fine. Edmondo, however, didn't wake up until several hours later, and thus the parasites had more time to grow inside him. When eventually persuaded to consume the drink, he expelled the parasites somewhat more violently than Federico had - he ended up taking a point of Lethal damage as he was rather violently puking up blood along with the parasites, which were significantly bigger than the ones Federico had thrown up. Anyways, he spent the rest of the day recovering in the healer's house while the rest of the party went off, and ultimately ended up taking care of a vampire who was living nearby. To cut a long story short, the vampire managed to fatally wound Xavier (our party's hunter) before dying, and we honestly thought he was going to die. However, Federico went and brought the healer to him, and to cut a long story short, she was able to (somehow - this is relevant very soon) completely heal his wounds.<br /> <br /> Anyways, upon returning to the village and tending to Edmondo once again, she informed him that the party had &quot;taken care of a nearby threat&quot; making no mention of what the &quot;threat&quot; was or the hunter's fatal wounds. Edmondo, deciding once again to engage in his Vice, offered to &quot;thank&quot; her for her services. Funnily enough, no Presence + Persuasion check was required this time, as it turned out that the healer was quite keen on Edmondo as well... and you can imagine what happened next. Anyways, the next day, when the party returned to the village, the healer was outed as a &quot;witch&quot; by Xavier, who was absolutely freaked out at th3e fact that she had somehow completely healed his fatal wound. She was captured, found guilty of witchcraft, and sentenced to burning at the stake. However, Edmondo, being the (somewhat) honorable man he was, made an attempt at persuading the crowd to not execute her for her &quot;crimes&quot;. Despite the fact that he ended up taking a penalty on the subsequent role for his &quot;Notorious&quot; condition for his... previous acts, he ended up getting an exceptional success, and somehow managed to talk the crowd out of executing her, instead persuading them to simply exile her from the village.<br /> <br /> Aaaaaanyways, that's a bit of a background on my character - I'll try and post more short stories about him and the rest of our party as the campaign goes on. If you have any questions about anything in the campaign, feel free to ask them here, and I'll answer them as best I can.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25006-123zane321","name":"123zane321","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"",